cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Equipoise"
abstract: >-
  Families of text generation compared at equal training compute, under one protocol, at small
  scale. Version 1.0 contains an independent small-scale reimplementation of the
  Energy-Based Transformer (EBT), studied on three tasks (regression with two correct answers,
  MNIST denoising and a character-level language model on Tiny Shakespeare) and compared with a
  baseline of the same size on each, at equal parameters and equal training steps. It asks seven
  questions on the EBT. Five are answered by their rules: faithful implementation, why use an
  energy, error against thinking steps, energy as a verifier and thinking out of distribution.
  The comparison at equal cost is answered in part, at equal parameters and equal steps only, and
  the training-component ablations were not run. The comparison of several families at equal
  compute is planned from version 1.1.
